    "body": "partial fix on issue/3646-multi-seat-cutters · PR #4192 · pinned by `the_tool_holds_the_real_cutter`, `a_face_mill_and_an_end_mill_share_one_insert`, `a_round_insert_end_mill_takes_half_its_insert_as_corner`, `the_assembled_face_mill_encloses_holder_and_body`, `degenerate_cutters_are_refused_by_name` · merges at the next cut\n\nThe PR is the `camcraft-tools` slice (Refs, not Fixes). Below 90 degrees the derived diameter is the reach of the edge, not `DC`, because a `DC` cylinder is smaller than the cutter. The decision file `docs/decisions/3646-multi-seat-cutters.md` gives the reason. The app part (the document record, the `Stale` marking after an edit of the shared insert, and the plunge and collision tests on an operation) waits for #3644.",
